{:edb/db-before-t 2056 :edb/db-after-t 2057 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535369 50 #inst "2026-10-08T22:59:18.645Z" 13194139535369 true] [17592186171969 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346206 13194139535369 true] [17592186171970 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346220 13194139535369 true] [17592186171970 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346227 13194139535369 true] [17592186171971 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346213 13194139535369 true] [17592186172571 1100 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" 13194139535369 true] [17592186172571 1100 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n2. At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n3. At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" 13194139535369 false] [17592186172571 1145 "First, we define $f(x,y)=2xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/6ef852c9c15dc6f591119906abe479949f929edb6dc26f21588b4de545d02da2.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\\,\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\\,\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\\,\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant." 13194139535369 true] [17592186172571 1145 "The factor $2$ is positive, so the sign of $2xy$ is the sign of $xy$. It is positive in quadrants I and III and negative in II and IV. Thus I and III are true, while II is false. Select **I and III only**." 13194139535369 false] [17592186346206 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346207 13194139535369 true] [17592186346206 1089 "q-119774" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346206 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535369 true] [17592186346206 1100 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=8{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346206 1113 #uuid "bd94ef21-a2a4-56ba-aab3-62f25fd6ae09" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346206 1145 "First, we define $f(x,y)=8{x}^{2}{y}^{2}.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/d1e4f48450a7f2032d755a5255d1a1e8a726dd16d273dae5dc1e587826d5ce58.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346208 13194139535369 true] [17592186346207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346209 13194139535369 true] [17592186346207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346210 13194139535369 true] [17592186346207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346211 13194139535369 true] [17592186346207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346212 13194139535369 true] [17592186346207 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535369 true] [17592186346207 1041 "selection" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346207 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346212 13194139535369 true] [17592186346207 1110 #uuid "16d73fc8-e01b-525a-8920-6d15cbb9db6c" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346208 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346208 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535369 true] [17592186346208 1111 #uuid "516139b1-0c44-5a73-bbcd-74968842ba7a" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346209 1034 "I only" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346209 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535369 true] [17592186346209 1111 #uuid "a7404818-5591-58aa-8264-23893dddbbe8" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346210 1034 "III only" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346210 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535369 true] [17592186346210 1111 #uuid "0e11e5f5-ffb7-5b65-b310-ece8db299f0f" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346211 1034 "None of those listed" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346211 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535369 true] [17592186346211 1111 #uuid "fd4c77b6-c609-5c2e-98d7-3491780ec88b" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346212 1034 "II only" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346212 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535369 true] [17592186346212 1111 #uuid "97beeffd-ec10-5cef-9ccc-8c7dac3b6ef1" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346213 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346214 13194139535369 true] [17592186346213 1089 "q-97534" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346213 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535369 true] [17592186346213 1100 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(x-1)(y-1)^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y<1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>1$ and $y<1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>1$ and $y>1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346213 1113 #uuid "9207fabe-2c1e-5522-9989-db0098e7f899" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346213 1145 "First, we define $f(x,y)=(x-1)(y-1)^{2}.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=1$ or $y=1.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/075264fa042adc64e160a83f03a2b125dd5a9b0927fc3ed318778c0004689ec4.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/5716d59a745fc148b504a4db523286d7c7209fe793fcf369a90d220125f7e9fb.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $x<1$ and $y<1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $x>1$ and $y<1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $x>1$ and $y>1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region." 13194139535369 true] [17592186346214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346215 13194139535369 true] [17592186346214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346216 13194139535369 true] [17592186346214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346217 13194139535369 true] [17592186346214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346218 13194139535369 true] [17592186346214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346219 13194139535369 true] [17592186346214 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535369 true] [17592186346214 1041 "selection" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346214 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346216 13194139535369 true] [17592186346214 1110 #uuid "0aa91f6d-b7a5-56fe-a6a3-90200d467108" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346215 1034 "I only" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346215 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535369 true] [17592186346215 1111 #uuid "6d408b37-044f-54cd-a51a-928a075e0d3c" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346216 1034 "III only" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346216 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535369 true] [17592186346216 1111 #uuid "eb53295e-af49-5343-b6f5-84fba66b3325" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346217 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346217 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535369 true] [17592186346217 1111 #uuid "99dc08f8-6370-5619-adb9-b2240ec54d72" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346218 1034 "None of those listed" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346218 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535369 true] [17592186346218 1111 #uuid "9cde33d4-299d-5e9c-9692-35abea4ae8ef" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346219 1034 "II only" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346219 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535369 true] [17592186346219 1111 #uuid "109290c1-fc89-5ffb-afe3-ec9f9cdf0221" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346220 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346221 13194139535369 true] [17592186346220 1089 "q-98229" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346220 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535369 true] [17592186346220 1100 "Given that $f(x,y)$ varies with both $x$ and $y,$ which of the following **cannot** be the slope field for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)?$" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346220 1113 #uuid "785c04b6-0c68-5e88-b598-3068a3e40899" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346220 1145 "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is a function of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the slope field varies with both $x$ and $y.$\n\nOf the given slope fields, we note the following slope field does not vary with $y$ given a fixed value of $x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/4ea9eceec3de9b414efa87954d869119caf0748f152186aff5ede9bbade3f1fc.png)\n\n \n\nTo see this more clearly, notice that if we draw a vertical line, the slopes do not vary.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/fe2169790c1ee1d823937235bedd20ff10ecca662f030fd03dbfe23434517e47.png)" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346222 13194139535369 true] [17592186346221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346223 13194139535369 true] [17592186346221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346224 13194139535369 true] [17592186346221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346225 13194139535369 true] [17592186346221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346226 13194139535369 true] [17592186346221 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535369 true] [17592186346221 1041 "selection" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346221 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346223 13194139535369 true] [17592186346221 1110 #uuid "adf7a2cd-078b-5100-b3d9-11599b6eb692" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346222 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/cb58d805bed05b6846fd0ab7657f8e05c65eb69562a6cda494689e44745fb9d1.png" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346222 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535369 true] [17592186346222 1111 #uuid "7b90fa3f-a7c8-5111-9f0b-292024a034ce" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346223 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/4ea9eceec3de9b414efa87954d869119caf0748f152186aff5ede9bbade3f1fc.png" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346223 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535369 true] [17592186346223 1111 #uuid "aae5858c-c671-58a8-99d9-e4122fd25837" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346224 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/d94451671073d38af905b1190a15f97e6419a3a6052f83e53caa5a94b4a7000a.png" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346224 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535369 true] [17592186346224 1111 #uuid "edf2ad87-441d-5cc6-9c51-29f68e4bf4bc" 13194139535369 true] [17592186346225 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/dif